2393       *#PPP# I may have misunderstood the code -
2394       	Is the outcome CHOB coded as ever/never in each exposure window?
2395       	How it is handled for participants who became obese in the middle of the window?
2396       	Would then then exposure in the latter half of the window happen after the outcome occur, causing reverse-causation?
2397       	I think we have discussed this before but don't remember exactly how we are going to do abou this.
2398       	Are you going to run model like this: chob_adol ~ exposure_preg + exposure_earlych + exposure_ch ?
2399       	Sorry for this silly question! ;
2400         /*BC:  Yes the outcome chob is coded as ever/never in each exposure window.
2401         When I was making the data from wide to long, I coded it so that when a participant became obese that time period and future time periods
2401     !  would  be excluded.
2402         Thus when I took the avg exposure for a particular window it didn't include any of the exposures from when a child became obese
2403         Does that make sense?
2404         And now that Andy suggested not adjusting for previous time periods, I am just running
2405         chob_adol ~ exposure_preg + covariates_preg
2406         chob_adol ~ exposure_earlych + covariates_earlych
2407         */
